markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Creating and Using Functions in JavaScript

#### Now that we know why functions are useful, let’s look at how to make one in JavaScript.

#### There are a few key steps:

## 🧩 **1. Give your function a name**
#### A function needs a name so you can refer to it later. Pick something that describes what the function does, like `showMessage` or `calculate_total`. In this example, we will use `addFive`.
#### *Remember in JavaScript we usually use camelCase for function names (like `addScore` or `changeColor`).
---



## 🔧 **2. Use the function keyword to define the function**
#### In JavaScript, a basic function starts with the word **function**, followed by the function’s name and parentheses `()` and curly braces `{}`.

#### The curly braces hold the code that will run when the function is called.

<img src="https://images.code.org/2ff33eae19cb46b985d53e915d6a41b0-image-1762380222918.png" alt="javascript creating a function called addfive" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## 🧱 **3. Write the code you want to run (inside the braces)**
#### The code inside the braces `{}` runs each time a function is called. 
#### You can put one line or many lines of code inside your function. 

<img src="https://images.code.org/9fa02e35402e2c0255a9e1ae638d4e3a-image-1762380282582.png" alt="Javascript code writing a function to add five and adjusting the total" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">

<div style="clear:both;"></div>


---

## ▶️ **4. Call the function to make it run**
#### Just defining a function doesn’t run it. You have to call it by typing its name with parentheses:

<img src="https://images.code.org/f23a8f9a41cc12b056ce8e9e245df2cc-image-1762380345396.png" alt="Python code defining a function reading def greet with an indented print statement saying hello world and then the function greet being called" width="450px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0 0 40px 10px;">


 
<div style="clear:both;"></div>

#### This code is calling the function in the **event listener**.

---

## Next up
#### In the next level, you will practice working with AI to debug the existing functions. 

MARKDOWN
